WEBVTT

NOTE
StoryCast: When Everything Goes Wrong. Original explainer.
Narration only (synthetic voice); the video has no music or other sound effects.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.311
The Hungarian Grand Prix,
the first of August, 2021.

2
00:00:06.811 --> 00:00:09.390
Rain fell shortly before the start.

3
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.345
Every car lined up on intermediate
tyres, built for a wet track.

4
00:00:14.445 --> 00:00:19.139
Lewis Hamilton started from pole,
with Valtteri Bottas alongside.

5
00:00:19.639 --> 00:00:23.310
On the run to Turn 1,
Bottas braked too late.

6
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.696
He hit Lando Norris, who was
pushed into Max Verstappen.

7
00:00:27.796 --> 00:00:30.739
Bottas then slid into Sergio Pérez.

8
00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:34.488
Further back, Lance Stroll
hit Charles Leclerc.

9
00:00:34.988 --> 00:00:40.334
After two laps behind the safety car,
the race was stopped under a red flag.

10
00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:43.503
During the pause, the track began to dry.

11
00:00:44.003 --> 00:00:47.730
Mercedes kept Hamilton
on intermediate tyres.

12
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.585
Every other car came into the
pit lane for slick tyres.

13
00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:56.520
Hamilton took the restart alone,
the only car on the starting grid.

14
00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.505
When Hamilton pitted for slicks,
Esteban Ocon took the lead.

15
00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:04.809
Sebastian Vettel stayed close behind him.

16
00:01:04.909 --> 00:01:09.245
Fernando Alonso held Hamilton
back for around ten laps.

17
00:01:09.745 --> 00:01:14.442
Ocon crossed the line first, for
his first Formula 1 victory.

18
00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:18.904
Vettel finished second on the
road, but was later disqualified.

19
00:01:19.004 --> 00:01:23.391
Officials could not obtain the
required fuel sample from his car.

20
00:01:23.491 --> 00:01:27.886
The official podium: Ocon,
Hamilton and Carlos Sainz.
